{"name":"Carriage Red","hex":"#8c403d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carriage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of conveying; carrying.","A means of conveyance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carriage"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carriage","blocks":[{"text":"A carriage is a two- or four-wheeled horse-drawn vehicle for passengers. Coaches are a special category within carriages; they are enclosed carriages with four corner posts and a fixed roof. From the early modern period until the rise of railways and motor vehicles, carriages were a principal means of road transport, with models ranging from simple vehicles to elaborate ceremonial coaches used by royalty. Although largely replaced by mechanized transport, carriages remain in use for ceremonial occasions, tourism, equestrian sport, and in some communities as everyday transport. Modern carriages have been redesigned and manufactured for sports such as combined driving and for tourist transport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Horse_of_Buckingham_Palace%2C_Londres_cropped_straightened.jpg/330px-Horse_of_Buckingham_Palace%2C_Londres_cropped_straightened.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carriage","wikidata":"Q235356"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg/500px-Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg/1280px-Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg/500px-Concours_national_d%27attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Competitive driving in France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AConcours_national_d'attelage_%C3%A9lite_Rennes_2014-1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Sal%C3%A3o_Nobre%2C_Museu_Nacional_dos_Coches%2C_Lisboa%2C_Portugal.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Sal%C3%A3o_Nobre%2C_Museu_Nacional_dos_Coches%2C_Lisboa%2C_Portugal.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th